# ── Binaries and executables ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.exe
lexer_app
syntax_analyzer
parser_app
src/**/*.exe
src/**/a.exe
src/**/lexer_app
src/**/syntax_analyzer

# NOTE: do not add a bare `src/**/parser` rule here. Git applies such a
# pattern to directories as well as files, so it matches the src/parser/
# SOURCE directory and silently hides parser.y, parser_lexer.l and their
# headers from version control. The only binaries this project builds are
# syntax_analyzer and lexer_app, both emitted to the project root and
# already covered above.

# ── Build objects ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.o
*.d
*.obj

# ── Flex & Bison generated files ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Matched by filename at any depth rather than by full path, so they stay
# ignored regardless of which directory layout the Makefiles use (these
# currently appear in src/parser/, and stale copies also exist in src/).
lex.yy.c
lex.yy.*.c
parser.tab.c
parser.tab.h
parser.output
location.hh
position.hh
stack.hh

# ── Test outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
out/

# ── Shell artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Makefiles use Windows-style `2>NUL` redirects. Under a POSIX shell that
# creates a file literally named NUL (containing the failed `move` message),
# regenerated on every build. It has been committed by accident before
# (see commit 6c001c5, "Delete src/NUL").
NUL

# ── System / Editor files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Phase Notes & Requirements Tracking (user configured) ───────────────────
implementation_plan.md
REQUIREMENTS.md
